  "Text": "On 21 May, battalion commander, Dzianis Prokharaŭ (call sign \"Kit\") announced that the battalion would become a regiment comprising two separate battalions. This was presented as \"a move to the next stage of building a [Belarusian] national military unit\" which \"tak[es] into account the scale of the tasks facing the Belarusian soldiers\". The regiment would consist of three battalions, \"Litvin\", \"Volat\", and \"Terror.\" Terror would later split from the Regiment and become an independent unit, the Terror Battalion.",
